  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-SLOTLESS-PROTECTIVE-CONTACT-OMISSION-001",
      "severity": "P2 provisional; source-derived missing equipment stress, impact and frequency unverified",
      "classification": "newly assessed 95e first-failure candidate; related to, but not the same contract as, a checkpoint 059 clothing receipt-admission record; global deduplication remains open",
      "detail": "The connected-player projection creates one entity per personal item, assigns its tactical inventory identity, ItemOf and optional ArmorItem, but inserts EquipSlot only for a Held left- or right-hand occupancy. InventoryView ItemQuery makes EquipSlot optional and armor_layer_chain can select a protective ArmorItem and retain its exact inventory ID without that component. EquipmentContactQuery instead requires &EquipSlot for every candidate row, even in the branch that matches the exact ArmorImpact inventory ID. The pinned Bevy ECS source requires that component for an &T query and combines tuple predicates conjunctively. Consequently a normally projected worn protective entity with no held occupancy and no later EquipSlot insertion can protect the wearer yet cannot be found by that contact query for its own positive armor impact.",
      "source_derived_example": "Authored linen_breeches has a worn placement with left/right leg base_clothing occupancies, positive protection and proximal coverage 0.94; the starting loadout also names it. Assuming an authorized party wearer has that exact selected placement, its connected occupancy reflects those authored rows, its entity and inventory ID are unique, no later system adds EquipSlot, and its layer is selected at left-leg surface coordinate 0.5, a positive non-avoided contact produces ArmorImpact carrying that ID. The source query excludes the slotless entity, so this function adds no defender equipment-contact entry for it. This is a conditional source trace, not a claimed executed encounter, observed receipt, or measured wear difference.",
